  "name": "AFP (ALFA-FETOPROTEIN)",
  "code": "AFP",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Parameter</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Normal Range (Adults)</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Increased AFP</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Decreased / Low AFP</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>AFP (Alpha-Fetoprotein)</strong></td>\n<td><strong>&lt; 10 ng/mL</strong> (some labs up to 20 ng/mL)</td>\n<td>- <strong>Liver cancer (Hepatocellular carcinoma)</strong> - <strong>Germ cell tumors</strong> (non-seminomatous testicular/ovarian tumors, yolk sac tumor) - <strong>Chronic liver diseases</strong> (hepatitis, cirrhosis &ndash; usually mild to moderate elevation) - <strong>Pregnancy</strong> (naturally elevated; used for maternal screening)</td>\n<td>- Usually not clinically significant in adults - In pregnancy, <strong>low maternal serum AFP</strong> may suggest <strong>chromosomal abnormalities (Down syndrome, trisomy 18)</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<ul>\n<li data-start=\"854\" data-end=\"971\">\n<p data-start=\"856\" data-end=\"971\">AFP is a <strong data-start=\"865\" data-end=\"889\">fetal plasma protein</strong> : normally present at high levels in the fetus, but very low in healthy adults.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"972\" data-end=\"1047\">\n<p data-start=\"974\" data-end=\"1047\">In <strong data-start=\"977\" data-end=\"987\">adults</strong>, it is mainly a <strong data-start=\"1004\" data-end=\"1020\">tumor marker</strong> (HCC, germ cell tumors).</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1048\" data-end=\"1268\">\n<p data-start=\"1050\" data-end=\"1129\">In <strong data-start=\"1053\" data-end=\"1066\">pregnancy</strong>, AFP testing (part of triple/quadruple screen) helps detect:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1132\" data-end=\"1268\">\n<li data-start=\"1132\" data-end=\"1215\">\n<p data-start=\"1134\" data-end=\"1215\"><strong data-start=\"1134\" data-end=\"1146\">High AFP</strong> : neural tube defects, abdominal wall defects, multiple gestation.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1218\" data-end=\"1268\">\n<p data-start=\"1220\" data-end=\"1268\"><strong data-start=\"1220\" data-end=\"1231\">Low AFP</strong> : Down syndrome, Edwards syndrome.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1269\" data-end=\"1402\">\n<p data-start=\"1271\" data-end=\"1402\">AFP levels must be interpreted <strong data-start=\"1302\" data-end=\"1346\">along with clinical findings and imaging</strong> (e.g., ultrasound, CT/MRI in liver cancer suspicion).</p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
